    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that sounds like a good start. for the sake of a well-rounded syllabus, i also want to mention some of the other perspectives students might bring up, like the idea that these wealth gaps are more about individual financial decisions or general market trends rather than just systemic policy. how should i frame those counter-arguments in the guide so the students know how they fit into the conversation?",
